   "website": "https://himalayanrescue.org.np",
   "aid_posts": "Aid posts at Pheriche (4,250 m) on the way to Everest and Manang (3,550 m), just before Thorung-la pass on the Annapurna circuit; staffed by volunteer doctors during spring and autumn. HRA also runs the Everest ER clinic at Everest Base Camp (5,350 m)."
  }
 },
 "insurance": {
  "source": "ntb_faq",
  "statement": "Helicopter services are available should you fall sick or meet with an accident while trekking. However, such rescue services are expensive. So comprehensive travel insurance is advised to cover emergencies like helicopter rescue and medical treatment.",
